hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16002","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, he said, Nahhaz ibn Judayy al-Hanafi narrated to me, from Sinan ibn Salamah, that his father narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the pots to be overturned on the day of Khaybar, and in them was the meat of the people's donkeys."
"16003","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham and Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Jawn ibn Qatadah, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a house at whose courtyard a waterskin was hanging, and he asked for drink, and it was said, it is from a dead animal, he said: The slaughtering of the skin is its tanning."
"16004","Amr ibn al-Haytham Abu Qatan narrated to us, he said, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Jawn ibn Qatadah, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Its tanning is its purification, or its slaughtering."
"16005","Waki narrated to us, he said, al-Fadl ibn Dalham narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Qabisah ibn Hurayth, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from me, take from me, Allah has made a way for them: the virgin with the virgin, one hundred lashes and exile for a year, and the non-virgin with the non-virgin, one hundred lashes and stoning."
"16006","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who has intercourse with the slavegirl of his wife, he said: If he coerced her, she is free, and he owes her the like of her, and if she obeyed him, she is his slave, and he owes her the like of her."
"16007","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Samad ibn Habib ibn Abd Allah al-Azdi, then al-Numayri, narrated to us, he said, Habib ibn Abd Allah, meaning his father, narrated to me, he said, I heard Sinan ibn Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq al-Hudhali narrating from his father, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a mount that brings him to satiety, let him fast Ramadan wherever it reaches him."
"16008","Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Nahhaz al-Hanafi, that Sinan ibn Salamah informed him, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the meat of the people's donkeys on the day of Khaybar, while it was in the pots, and it was overturned."
